      "side": 1,
      "message": "I noticed that this CL also changes the range encoder in entenc.c and entenc.h. I have been working on the same code for real time screen encoding and uploaded my change as https://aomedia-review.googlesource.com/c/aom/+/219321. It keeps the coder state in local variables over a whole transform block, and the output stays bit exact. In my tests at RT speed 11 on screen content, the encoder was 2% to 6% faster, for both 4:2:0 and 4:4:4.\n\nThe two changes touch the same lines, so I wanted to ask how you would prefer to handle it. One option could be to move the entropy coder part into a separate CL, so the two approaches can be compared on their own. I\u0027m also happy to rebase my change on top of yours, or to adapt it if you see a better way.",
